{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "dearlys-api-collection",
    "name": "Dearly's API",
    "description": "REST API for Dearly's e-commerce backend.\n\n## Base URL\n`{{baseUrl}}` (default: http://localhost:5001/api/v1)\n\n## Authentication\nProtected routes use an HTTP-only cookie named `access_token` set by **Auth → Login** or **Register**.\n\nIn Postman: enable cookies (cookie jar). Call Login first; the cookie is sent on later requests.\n\n## Addresses\n- `GET/POST /addresses` and `GET/POST /users/me/addresses` are equivalent (auth required).\n- First saved address is auto-set `isDefault: true`.\n- `PATCH .../addresses/:id/default` or `PATCH .../users/me/addresses/:id/default` sets the default shipping address.\n\n## Orders\n`POST /orders` requires `addressId` — must belong to the logged-in user. Cart must be non-empty.\n\n## Admin product images\n`POST /admin/products` accepts `multipart/form-data` with file field `images` (up to 10) plus text fields (`name`, `category`, `price`, etc.). JSON fields like `inventory` can be sent as JSON strings.\n\n## Admin routes\nRequire role `ADMIN` (auth middleware may be disabled in dev — check `admin.routes.js`).\n\n## Response shape\n```json\n{ \"success\": true, \"message\": \"...\", \"data\": { ... } }\n```",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
